  "worked_solution": "Notice that our solid can be written as a type II region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,-1\\le x\\le 3{y}^{2}+3{z}^{2}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={\u222d}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{3{y}^{2}+3{z}^{2}}dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[x]_{x=-1}^{x=3{y}^{2}+3{z}^{2}}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3{y}^{2}+3{z}^{2}-(-1)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3{y}^{2}+3{z}^{2}+1\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[(3{y}^{2}+1)z+{z}^{3}]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(3{y}^{2}+1)(1)+{1}^{3}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3{y}^{2}+2\\,dy \\\\  & =[{y}^{3}+2y]_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & ={1}^{3}+2(1)-0 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$",
